<script>
import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Exchange from '#src/lib/Exchange.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={['/app/on-health', '/middleware/middleware', '/ambients/server']}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/app.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('/__abide/health answers the account, the app winning collisions",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/ops/lib/Health.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('the health check carries the database beside the baseline'",
            ],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Point a load balancer at the health check">
        <p>Every app answers <code>GET /__abide/health</code> with no handler written. A change in
            <code>startedAt</code> between two scrapes is a restart. The endpoint passes through the
            app's middleware, so a rung that refuses anonymous callers has to let it through.</p>
        <Code code={`
            $ curl localhost:3000/__abide/health
            {"version":"1.4.0","abide":"0.9.2","startedAt":"2026-11-19T08:00:00.000Z"}
        `} />
        <p>The CRM's, asked when this page loaded. Its <code>database</code> field is the one its root layout
            adds with <code>onHealth</code>.</p>
        <Exchange path="/__abide/health" />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Report the database beside the baseline">
        <p>Return the field from <code>onHealth</code> in the root layout. Your fields win a
            collision with the baseline's, and <code>onHealth</code>'s page shows how to type
            them.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <script server>
            import { onHealth } from '@abide/abide/server'
            import { pool } from './lib/pool.server.ts'

            onHealth(() => ({ database: pool.connected ? 'connected' : 'closed' }))
            </script>
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Show the account on an operations page">
        <p><code>health</code> is a handler that takes no arguments, called the same way on both
            sides.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <script>
            import { computed, health } from '@abide/abide'

            const account = computed(() => health())
            </script>

            <p>Up since {account.startedAt}, database {account.database}</p>
        `} />
    </Section>
</Doc>
